{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Wind Gusts",
 "category": "Effects",
 "text": "Sound: wind: gusting, howling, rising and falling by itself. No pitch at all, only filtered noise.\n\nHow it's built: white noise through the State-Variable filter's band-pass with some RESONANCE (the howl); a slow Smooth random LFO moves its CUTOFF (the gusts) and a second one moves the volume through a VCA. A narrow band of noise is quiet, so Drive brings it up (and roughens the howl); a Reverb.\n\nPlay: hold any key; let go and the wind dies down.\n\nTweak: the LFOs' RATEs (calm to storm), RESONANCE (more is a whistling howl), the filter's CV.",
